.TH "ALTFSCHANGER" "8" "15 November 2026" "LTFS" "LTFS Command Reference"

.SH NAME
altfschanger \- Drive a tape library's medium changer through a changer plugin
.SH SYNOPSIS

\fBaltfschanger\fR [ \fB-e \fIname\fB\fR ] [ \fB-i \fIfile\fB\fR ] \fBlist\fR


\fBaltfschanger\fR \fB-d \fIname\fB\fR [ \fB-e \fIname\fB\fR ] [ \fB-i \fIfile\fB\fR ] [ \fB-o \fIoption\fB\fR ] [ \fB--verbose=\fInum\fB\fR ] \fB\fIcommand\fB\fR [ \fB\fIargument\fB\fR\fI ...\fR ]

.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
\fBaltfschanger\fR sends single operations to the medium changer of a tape
library through a changer plugin: it reads the element status, moves and exchanges
cartridges between element addresses, and makes the changer re-read its elements. It is
a tool for testing the changer plugins and for driving a library by hand; it keeps no
state between runs.
.PP
Elements are named by their address as the changer reports it. The library is shared
with its operator panel and with other hosts, and \fBaltfschanger\fR does
not reserve it: check the element status before a move.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB-d, --device=\fIname\fB\fR
The medium changer. Its form depends on the plugin: for the file
plugin, a library directory, or the name or serial number of a library directory
under the directory that the environment variable
\fBALTFS_FILE_CHANGER_ROOT\fR names.
.TP
\fB-e, --backend=\fIname\fB\fR
Use the specified changer plugin (default: the default changer of the configuration file)
.TP
\fB-i, --config=\fIfile\fB\fR
Use the specified configuration file
.TP
\fB-o \fIoption\fB\fR
Pass an option to the changer plugin; \fBaltfschanger help\fR lists them
.TP
\fB--verbose=\fInum\fB\fR
Set the log level: 0 errors, 1 warnings, 2 informational (the default),
3 to 6 debug.
.TP
\fB-h, --help\fR
Show the usage
.TP
\fB-V, --version\fR
Show the version
.SH "COMMANDS"
.TP
\fBlist\fR
List the medium changers this host can reach
.TP
\fBinfo\fR
Show the identity of the changer, its element address assignment and whether it reads barcodes, reports drive serial numbers and accepts EXCHANGE MEDIUM
.TP
\fBelements [\fItype\fB [\fIstart\fB [\fIcount\fB]]]\fR
Show the element status, one element per line: type, address, full or empty,
then voltag= (the barcode), source=,
dvcid= (the drive serial number) and the flags
inaccessible, except=\fIASC\fR/\fIASCQ\fR
and impexp\&. \fItype\fR is
transport, storage, ie,
drive or any (the default).
.TP
\fBmove \fIsource\fB \fIdest\fB [\fItransport\fB]\fR
MOVE MEDIUM from one element address to another
.TP
\fBexchange \fIsource\fB \fIdest1\fB \fIdest2\fB [\fItransport\fB]\fR
EXCHANGE MEDIUM: the cartridge at \fIsource\fR goes to \fIdest1\fR and the one at \fIdest1\fR goes to \fIdest2\fR, which may be \fIsource\fR
.TP
\fBscan [\fIstart\fB \fIcount\fB]\fR
Make the changer re-read its elements (INITIALIZE ELEMENT STATUS); on a large library this takes minutes
.TP
\fBtur\fR
Send TEST UNIT READY
.TP
\fBprevent, allow\fR
Lock or unlock the import/export station
.TP
\fBhelp\fR
Show the options of the changer plugin
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.PP
0 on success, 8 when the operation failed (the message ACH0004E gives
the internal error code), 16 for a usage error.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.PP
altfs(8), mkaltfs(8).
